tures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use when the user asks how to build with OpenAI products or APIs and needs up-to-date official documentation with citations, help choosing the latest model for a use case, or model upgrade and prompt-upgrade guidance; prioritize OpenAI docs MCP tools, use bundled references only as helper context, and restrict any fallback browsing to official OpenAI domains. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-creator: Create and scaffold plugin directories for Codex with a required `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`, optional plugin folders/files, and baseline placeholders you can edit before publishing or testing. Use when Codex needs to create a new local plugin, add optional plugin structure, or generate or update repo-root `.agents/plugins/marketplace.json` entries for plugin ordering and availability metadata. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/plugin-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Codex's capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo (including private repos). (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- brainstormer: Partner with the user to turn rough ideas into well-structured concepts, then help evaluate and refine them. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/brainstormer/SKILL.md)\n- code-reviewer: Review code changes with an emphasis on correctness, clarity, maintainability, and test coverage. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/code-reviewer/SKILL.md)\n- committer: Prepare clear, scoped commit messages and help organize changes into coherent commits. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/committer/SKILL.md)\n- context-fetcher: Gather the minimum relevant context needed to begin work without overwhelming the user with unnecessary detail. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/context-fetcher/SKILL.md)\n- deep-research: Conduct deeper multi-step research, synthesis, and comparison when the user needs more than a quick answer. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/deep-research/SKILL.md)\n- deployment-reporter: Summarize deployment outcomes, risks, rollback considerations, and next checks in a way that is easy for teams to act on. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/deployment-reporter/SKILL.md)\n- docs-maintainer: Improve or create documentation so it is accurate, structured, and easy for the intended audience to use. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/docs-maintainer/SKILL.md)\n- entire:explain: Explains the intent behind source code by finding original session transcripts. Use /explain with a function, file, or line of code to understand why it exists. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/personal-local/entire/0.1.0/skills/explain/SKILL.md)\n- entire:search: Use when the user wants to find prior work, checkpoints, or agent conversations by topic, repo, branch, author, or recent time window (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/personal-local/entire/0.1.0/skills/search/SKILL.md)\n- entire:session-handoff: Use when 