file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/github/f812c146/skills/github/SKILL.md)\n- github:yeet: Publish local changes to GitHub by confirming scope, committing intentionally, pushing the branch, and opening a draft PR through the GitHub app from this plugin, with `gh` used only as a fallback where connector coverage is insufficient. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/github/f812c146/skills/yeet/SKILL.md)\n- pr-prep: Prepare code changes for pull request submission with a focus on clarity, scope, and reviewer usability. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/pr-prep/SKILL.md)\n- product-developer: Build product features with a pragmatic balance of user needs, technical constraints, and iteration speed. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/product-developer/SKILL.md)\n- project-shipper: Drive work toward completion by clarifying scope, sequencing execution, and focusing on what is necessary to ship. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/project-shipper/SKILL.md)\n- rapid-prototyper: Help build fast, rough implementations to validate ideas quickly before investing in polish. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/rapid-prototyper/SKILL.md)\n- retro-writer: Turn project or incident history into a clear retrospective with lessons, decisions, and concrete follow-ups. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/retro-writer/SKILL.md)\n- scaffold-builder: Create initial project or feature scaffolding that gives the user a strong starting point without overengineering. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/scaffold-builder/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:brainstorming: You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requirements and design before implementation. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/brainstorming/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:dispatching-parallel-agents: Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/dispatching-parallel-agents/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:executing-plans: Use when you have a written implementation plan to execute in a separate session with review checkpoints (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/executing-plans/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch: Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work - guides completion of development work by presenting structured options for merge, PR, or cleanup (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/finishing-a-development-branch/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:receiving-code-review: Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing suggestions, especially if feedback seems unclear or technically questionable - requires technical rigor and verification, not performative agreement or blind implementation (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/receiving-code-review/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:requesting-code-review: Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/requesting-code-review/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:subagent-driven-development: Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/subagent-driven-development/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:systematic-debugging: Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/systematic-debugging/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:test-driven-development: Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/test-driven-development/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:using-git-worktrees: Use when starting feature work that needs isolation from current workspace or before executing implementation plans - creates isolated git worktrees with smart directory selection and safety verification (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/using-git-worktrees/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:using-superpowers: Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:verification-before-completion: Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/verification-before-completion/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:writing-plans: Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/writing-plans/SKILL.md)\n- superpowers:writing-skills: Use when creating new skills, editing existing skills, or verifying skills work before deployment (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/superpowers/skills/writing-skills/SKILL.md)\n- test-writer: Add or improve tests with a focus on meaningful coverage, edge cases, and long-term maintainability. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/test-writer/SKILL.md)\n- ux-evaluator: Evaluate a user flow, interface, or experience and surface practical improvements with clear rationale. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/ux-evaluator/SKILL.md)\n### How to use skills\n- Discovery: The list above is the skills available in this session (name + description + file path). Skill bodies live on disk at the listed paths.\n- Trigger rules: If the user names a skill (with `$SkillName` or plain text) OR the task clearly matches a skill's description shown above, you must